  "notes": "Uptown bad-boy gospel-R&B under DeVanté Swing's raw, church-derived production, 1991–1996. The research reads \"56–70 half-time ballads (reads 112–140) + 86–93 straight uptempo\" and names F minor as the signature key across four sourced titles, so the felt half-time spine is the base and `keys` is weighted onto Fm with Cm and Gm secondary. The three drum deltas are quoted from the entry: kick \"on 1 and the 8th before 3\" with nothing else (density 1–2, syncopation almost off), \"clap/snare on beat 3 of the doubled grid\" (`halftime_3`, a clap layer, no ghost habit), and \"almost no hat pattern; where hats appear they are 16ths at low velocity\" (16th base, not continuous, fill density 0.1, velocities at a third of the parent's). Harmony is \"gospel quartet voicing — minor 7ths, sus4 resolutions, 9ths in the pad; two- and four-bar vamps\", which is the `susSubstitutionProb` lift, the seventh/ninth-heavy extension spread and the two-chord families; \"no countermelody\" is why the counter density drops to the floor of what still generates rather than being deleted. The bass is \"long-sustaining synth bass that holds the root through the whole bar, minimal movement… deliberately loud\" — hence a near-1.0 root-follow, one note per cell and no passing motion. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity, density and register numbers and `swing.amount` 0.50; the entry's machine lineage is marked `[LOW-CONF, genre-level]` and no field encodes it.",
